From: Jonathan Jackson <70459+jjackson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:24:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Labs mode: key a user's sandbox by HQ server

The user sandbox (dbs/<domain>/<user>, its app dbs, the case-search temp db) and
the Redis last-sync-time key were keyed by domain and username only, so the same
domain and username on www and eu would share cases and a sync token. A labs
request naming a non-default HQ server (X-Labs-HQ-Host) now uses
<domain>@<host slug> for both (RequestUtils.getSandboxDomain). An X-Labs-HQ-Host
equal to commcarehq.host counts as no host, so default-server workers keep one
sandbox whether or not labs sends the header. Non-labs requests are unchanged.
